# Civilization VII on iPhone Duo — handheld 1080p, native aspect and touch findings

Test report for NX2Apple v1.5.0-rc8 on iPhone Duo, iOS 27.2, built with Xcode 27.2 on an Apple silicon Mac.

- Engine ID 94a0944755da1a443f42651bf7ee49ab24ed5ee5-d599bd14eb6d.
- Title 0100C3601518C000, package v1638400, profile version 1.5.0.1.
- main build ID 5d9401301ab2bb4917bafd939e5b3dd8.
- Shader chain b-19d183a2b462.

## Handheld 1080p

The game initializes Switch_Handheld_Validation and Switch_Docked_Validation profiles. Handheld loads a 1280×720 literal at main+0x48af9a8. Docked loads 1920×1080 at main+0x48aef60. The handheld load writes dimensions to profile offset +0x14.

Two build-specific cuts redirected the handheld load to the existing docked size literal:

    CUTS = {'5d9401301ab2bb4917bafd939e5b3dd8': [
        (0x904e8, 'e94002f0', 'e94002d0', 'handheld literal page'),
        (0x904f8, '20d544fd', '20b147fd', 'handheld 1920x1080 dimensions'),
    ]}

Logs confirmed DM_OPMODE=0, a 1920×1080 swapchain and matching WindowCrop. Downstream forced-size experiments either reverted to 720p or caused a null resource lookup, and were withdrawn.

## Gesture mapping

Civ7 reads GetGestureStates. A zero GetTouchScreenState call count did not establish that touch was absent. In fixed Tap layout, logs recorded Touch→Tap→Complete, Press and Pinch. With the 1080p profile, pinch worked but buttons did not respond correctly.

Scaling outgoing gesture positions, points, deltas and velocities by 1.5 restored interaction in the player's test. Recognition history and thresholds stayed in 1280×720 coordinates. Gesture type, direction, flags, rotation and pinch scale were preserved. The local opt-in switch was DM_CIV7_GESTURE_SCALE=1.5.

## Native Duo aspect

A further experiment changed output to 1920×1344 and included a game-specific swapchain stub. Swapchain, crop, render targets and full scissor followed the taller dimensions. Despite that, the host reported picture shape 1920×1080 to the iOS front end.

In nvn_mtl.m, present_shape() falls back to a 1920×1080 layer when neither the screen shape nor layer shape supplies the intended aspect. A local, game-specific experiment returned src.width and src.height only for an explicitly enabled 1920×1344 source texture. Logs then reported picture shape 1920×1344 (1.429:1), and the player confirmed full-screen gameplay.

For the taller output, a separate outgoing Y scale of 1344/720 was installed while retaining X scale 1920/1280. The player subsequently accepted the adjusted full-screen interaction and HUD placement. Exhaustive UI and long-duration regression coverage remain incomplete. Uniform 1.5 scaling is the explicitly accepted 1080p touch baseline.

## Optional UI polish

A per-game RomFS overlay was used for larger top-bar text/icons and safe insets. The actual pause/menu button is panel-system-button with radial-tag ps-bar-pause inside .ps-content-wrapper. Outer panel margins did not reliably reposition it. The player accepted the later HUD placement.

A blue-gray strip appearing only in the main menu matched the .motd-box background #333640. Making this background transparent for the unfolded aspect removed it in a device screenshot.

## Validation limits and integration

These findings combine logs, screenshots and player interaction tests. Long-duration stability, all UI states, camera field of view/culling and independent reproduction against a clean engine are pending. The engine inherited earlier Tap-layout and gesture-enabling changes plus diagnostics, whose individual necessity has not been isolated.

A reviewed title-specific profile and presentation-shape integration would be preferable to an unconditional change for every game, since anamorphic presentation must remain supported. The local switches above are experiments, not upstream features. CSS changes are optional accessibility preferences.

This report includes no game files, keys, credentials, private paths or raw device containers.


Submission target

NX2Apple CONTRIBUTING.md routes game profiles, runtime graphics and control fixes to seedds/nxnative. This package is an integration candidate tested with an NX2Apple rc8 engine fork; clean-upstream reproduction and automated regression tests remain pending.


