### Symptom

Hades II (0100A00019DE0000, v655360) on an iPhone 15 Pro Max: on the save-slot screen, switching to handheld from the in-game menu and back to docked leaves the game taking no input at all, from the touch gamepad or a controller. The game keeps running; only the input is gone, until the app restarts.

### Cause

`dm_set_opmode` moves player 1 between the Handheld npad and No1 (`connected_id`), as docking takes the Joy-Cons off the console's rails or puts them back, and pushes notification 30. It never signals the npads' style update events. On the console the hid service signals both npads, and the game re-reads which npad has a controller. Here, Hades II's input layer kept reading the npad it had moved to, Handheld, which is empty once docked.

`BindNpadStyleSetUpdateEvent` also kept events only for No1..No8 (`*id < DM_PLAYERS`), so an event bound to Handheld (0x20) could not be signalled at all.

### Fix

The style events get a Handheld slot, and a console mode change signals No1 and Handheld before the notification is pushed:

