#### Diagnostic findings :
Looking at the logs around the swapchain transition:
- The game presents ticket `#3` for `ser=2` via `nvnQueuePresentTexture`.
- Right after queuing ticket `#3`, the main thread destroys the splash swapchain: calling `nvnTextureFinalize` on `ser=2` and `ser=3`, followed by `nvnWindowInitialize` with the game swapchain (`ser=7, 8`).
- Because presentation processing is asynchronous on the display link thread, by the time ticket `#3` is presented in `present_now`, `ser=2` has already been finalized by `mtl_tex_release(TX(t))` and deleted from `g_by_serial`.
- In `tex_mtl_`: `tex_get(2)` returns `nil`. Because there is no check whether a non-cached serial is still live in `g_tex_live`, a new `MTLTexture` is allocated on the display thread. Since `tex_zero_fill` only runs on the submit thread, this allocation contains uninitialized GPU memory, which samples as magenta (`#f833f8`) when presented.
- If `tex_mtl_` returns `nil` when a non-cached serial is no longer in `g_tex_live`, `present_now`'s existing `if (!src) return 0;` cleanly drops the stale ticket without acquiring or presenting a drawable, eliminating the flash.

#### locally tested possible fix:
```diff
--- a/dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m
+++ b/dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m
@@ -3298,4 +3298,8 @@ static id<MTLTexture> tex_mtl_(const tex_t *ct) {
     id have = tex_get(t->serial);
+    if (!have) {
+        pthread_mutex_lock(&g_smu); int live = t->serial >= (1ull << 62) || nvn_hm_get(&g_tex_live, &t->serial) != NULL; pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_smu);
+        if (!live) { RED_ONCE(71, "texture ser=%llu is no longer live: no MTLTexture created", (unsigned long long)t->serial); return nil; }
+    }
     if (!packaged && !have && DM_GAME_TEX_DIRTY_UPLOAD && t->mem && on_sub_thread()) { int nvn_ft_written(const tex_t *); packaged = nvn_ft_written(t); }
```

With this change, the stale ticket is detected and dropped cleanly, completely eliminating the magenta flash:
```text
